From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Writer tracked changes carry their words

- The tracked-change list gave only a description in the kernel's
  fixed English ("Insert “…”"), so ElyDoc could not quote a change's
  words in its own language (R23.7, #125).
- Each entry of getCommandValues(".uno:AcceptTrackedChanges") gains
  "text": the changed words, shortened as the description shortens
  them (GetDescr(true)).

diff --git a/sw/source/uibase/uno/unotxdoc.cxx b/sw/source/uibase/uno/unotxdoc.cxx
--- a/sw/source/uibase/uno/unotxdoc.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/uibase/uno/unotxdoc.cxx
@@ -3531,6 +3531,8 @@
         rJson.put("comment",
                            rRedlineTable[i]->GetRedlineData().GetComment());
         rJson.put("description", rRedlineTable[i]->GetDescr());
+        // The changed words alone, for Ely's card.
+        rJson.put("text", rRedlineTable[i]->GetDescr(true));
         OUString sDateTime = utl::toISO8601(
             rRedlineTable[i]->GetRedlineData().GetTimeStamp().GetUNODateTime());
         rJson.put("dateTime", sDateTime);
